\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 13, 2010\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in the Closed Session Conference Room, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r Initiation of Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(c): one case.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:00 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:15 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Bingham, Colantuono, Coroalles, Davidoo, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Sarah Sherman and Justin Field.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the City Council added two additional items of Initiation of Litigation to the closed session agenda and that there was no reportable action in closed session.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\r Councilmember Bozajian and Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding Monty Fisher and Barry Bernholtz, in whose memory the meeting is being adjourned. Councilmember Maurer provided a reminder about the City�s monthly electronic waste round-up. Mayor Wolfson announced the upcoming Snow, Snow, Snow Day that will be taking place on Sunday, January 31, 2010. Councilmember Maurer welcomed students from New Community Jewish High School who are attending tonight�s meeting. Mayor Wolfson announced that the annual State of the City address and Chamber Mixer will be occuring on Wednesday, January 20, 2010 in Founders Hall. \r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT:\r\rGary Klein, Calabasas, spoke regarding the different standards of measuring building heights. Mary Hubbard, representing the Malibu Canyon Community Association, spoke in opposition to the proposed pervious surface requirements. Craig Overstock, Calabasas, requested clarification on one issue with the proposed development code.\r\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of meeting minutes from December 9, 2009. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1214, proclaiming March 20, 2010 as �Arbor Day� in the City of Calabasas.�� \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1215, requesting the Board of Supervisors of the Los Angeles County Flood Control District of the State of California to accept on behalf of said district the transfer and conveyance of the storm drain improvements known as Private Drain 2092 in the City of Calabasas for future operation, maintenance, repair and improvement, and authorize the transfer and conveyance thereof. \r\r Authorization to approve an extension of the Venco Western, Inc. contracts for one year for Specification No. 05-06-02 landscape maintenance of the common areas within individual homeowner associations and common benefit areas within Landscape Maintenance District 22. \r\r Authorization to approve an amendment to extend an existing professional service agreement with Marine Biochemists of California and approve budgeted funding to cover the annual cost of maintaining Calabasas Lake and repair or replacement of lake aeration equipment. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1217, supporting the application by the City of Calabasas for the Energy Efficiency and Conservation Block Grant Program administered by the United States Department of Energy. \r \rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, and 6 with a minor revision to the minutes of December 9, 2009. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve Consent Item 5. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rPUBLIC HEARINGS \r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING: Consideration and certification of a mitigated negative declaration, and introduction of Ordinance No. 2010-265 amending the City of Calabasas development code and zoning map to bring these documents into conformance with the policies and programs of the City of Calabasas 2030 General Plan, as recommended by the Planning Commission and pursuant to Calabasas Municipal Code Chapter 17.76.\r\r Tom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report.\r\r Councilmember Maurer stated for the record that she opposes vineyards as an agricultural use for environmental reasons and opposes storage units in scenic highways and corridors.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2010-265, amending the City of Calabasas development code and zoning map to bring these documents into conformance with the policies and programs of the City of Calabasas 2030 General Plan, as recommended by the Planning Commission and pursuant to Calabasas Municipal Code Chapter 17.76. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Consideration and certification of a negative declaration and introduction of Ordinance No. 2010-268, approving amendments to Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code � Construction and Building.\r\r Mayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\r Anita Davidoo, Associate Engineer, presented the staff report.\r Mayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2010-268, approving amendments to Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code � Construction and Building. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Review and approval of projects for the 36th program year (2010-2011) - Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) funding; and Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1216, approving the CDBG 36th program year (2010-2011) - to the 1/13/10 Council Agenda.\r\r Mayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\r John Bingham, Senior Management Analyst, presented the staff report.\r Mayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to adopt Resolution No. 2010-1216, approving the CDBG 36th program year (2010-2011), specifically approving option 2, which is the reinstatement of the residential rehabilitation program. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2010-267, amending the Calabasas Municipal Code to require encroachment permits for major construction projects within the Old Topanga Overlay Zone, the Calabasas Highlands Overlay Zone and the Park Moderne Overlay Zone. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2010-267, amending the Calabasas Municipal Code to require encroachment permits for major construction projects within the Old Topanga Overlay Zone, the Calabasas Highlands Overlay Zone and the Park Moderne Overlay Zone with revisions to items (iii) and (iv) of Section 2 to change the project size to 400 square feet. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of December 2, 2009 to December 29, 2009. \r\r There was no action taken. \r\rTHE CITY COUNCIL RECESSED TO CALABASAS EDUCATION FUND BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r The City Manager indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested the following items be placed on a future agenda:\r\rReview of the parking code, specifically to investigate allowing tandem parking in certain instances; \rA presentation by Dr. Zimring to address compliance with school permit requirements; \rDiscussion regarding restricting tobacco sales near schools.\r\r\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:03 p.m. in memory of Monty Fisher and Barry Bernholtz to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, January 27, 2010 at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00144\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r01/13/10\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u